SET INTERNING TEST HOOKS
========================

The following fault injector exists only when the VMOD was configured with both ``--enable-set-interning`` and ``--enable-test-hooks``. It verifies the fail-closed allocation path of the experimental implementation and must not be exposed in a production build.

$Method BOOL .test_fail_next_intern_alloc()

One-shot: fail the next interned membership-set allocation; the affected attach fails closed.

$Method BOOL .test_intern_initial_buckets(INT buckets)

Set the lazy set-interning table's initial bucket count for regression tests.

$Method BOOL .test_fail_next_intern_table_alloc()

Make the next set-interning bucket-array allocation fail.

$Method INT .test_intern_migration_active()

Return ``1`` while a retiring set-interning table is retained.

$Method BOOL .test_intern_worker_hold(BOOL hold)

Pause or resume automatic set-interning migration maintenance.

$Method INT .test_intern_migrate_buckets(INT buckets)

Advance a set-interning migration by at most ``buckets`` steps, capped at the normal request-side migration budget.

$Method INT .test_intern_active_buckets()

Return the active set-interning bucket count.

$Method INT .test_intern_old_buckets()

Return the retiring set-interning bucket count.
